## Setup Instructions (start to finish)

### 1. Prerequisites

```powershell
# Install Node.js (LTS) if not already installed
# Download from https://nodejs.org — version 20+ recommended
node -v   # confirm installation
npm -v
```

### 2. Create the project

```powershell
cd "d:\job search\Self-Learn\Portfolio"
npm create vite@latest ./ -- --template react
npm install
```

### 3. Install dependencies

```powershell
npm install bootstrap react-bootstrap react-icons aos
```

### 4. Run dev server

```powershell
npm run dev
# Opens at http://localhost:5173
```

### 5. Build for production

```powershell
npm run build
# Output goes to dist/
```

---

## Free Deployment — GitHub Pages

### Option A: GitHub Pages (recommended — 100% free)

1. Create a GitHub repo (e.g. `portfolio`).
2. Install the deploy helper:
   ```powershell
   npm install --save-dev gh-pages
   ```
3. Add to `package.json` → `scripts`:
   ```json
   "predeploy": "npm run build",
   "deploy": "npx gh-pages -d dist"
   ```
4. Add `base` to `vite.config.js`:
   ```js
   export default defineConfig({
     base: '/portfolio/',   // ← must match repo name
     plugins: [react()],
   })
   ```
5. Deploy:
   ```powershell
   npm run deploy
   ```
6. Your site is live at **`https://<username>.github.io/portfolio/`**.

### Option B: Vercel (also free)

1. Push repo to GitHub.
2. Go to [vercel.com](https://vercel.com), sign in with GitHub.
3. Import the repo → Vercel auto-detects Vite → click **Deploy**.
4. Live URL is assigned automatically (custom domain supported).

### Option C: Netlify (also free)

1. Push repo to GitHub.
2. Go to [netlify.com](https://netlify.com), connect repo.
3. Build command: `npm run build`, publish dir: `dist`.
4. Deploy.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> GitHub Pages is simplest for a personal portfolio. Vercel/Netlify are great if you later add a backend or serverless functions.

